==Japanese==
{{ja-kanjitab|左|利}}

===Etymology 1===
/hidarikiki/: [pidarikiki] > [ɸidarikiki] > [çidarikiki]. Compound of {{term|左|hidari|left}} and {{term|利き|kiki|effective}}. See {{term|左利き|hidarigiki}}.

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|kk|hira=ひだりきき|rom=hidarikiki}}

# the ability to use a left hand better than a right hand; [[left-handedness]]
# a person who can use their left hand better than their right hand; [[left-handed]] [[person]]

===Etymology 2===
/hidarigiki/: [pidarigiki] > [ɸidarigiki] > [çidarigiki]. Compound of {{term|左|hidari|left}} and {{term|利き|kiki|effective}}. /kiki/ voices to [giki] due to [[w:Rendaku|compounding]].

====Noun====
{{ja-noun|kk|hira=ひだりぎき|rom=hidarigiki}}

# the ability to use a left hand better than a right hand; [[left-handedness]]
# a person who can use their left hand better than their right hand; [[left-handed]] [[person]]
#* {{RQ:Nippo Jisho|229}}
#*: '''Fidariguiqi'''. ヒダリギキ (左利き) 左利きの人.

[[Category:Rendaku|ひだりぎき]]

